# AudioManager (required)

`AudioManager` is the **only** voice-control module.

## Game / UI API

- `playBgm(stage)` · `stopBgm()` · `playSe(id)` · `setGameState(state)` · `dispose()`
- Do **not** use `AudioContext`, timers, or oscillators from game code
- Prefer `setGameState("playing" | "clear" | "pause" | "menu")` over manual stop/start chains

## BGM

- Exactly **one** instance
- State machine: `stopped → starting → playing → stopping → stopped`
- `pendingStage` holds the **latest** request only (no FIFO) — rapid `playBgm(3/5/9)` ends on 9
- Generation tokens cancel stale starts (no double play / leftover tempo)

## Lifecycle

- Call `dispose()` on screen unmount so timers, oscillators, gains, and AudioContext are released
- Remount is safe — `unlock()` recreates the context

AudioManagerは唯一の音声制御モジュールとし、ゲーム側はAudioContext・Timer・Oscillatorを直接操作しないでください。AudioManagerは状態機械として動作し、BGMは常に1インスタンスのみ管理します。また、dispose() を実装し、画面破棄時にすべての音声リソースを確実に解放してください。

## Volume (future — do not implement in Binary Block Phase 1)

When settings / mute polish / mobile / app builds need it, extend **AudioManager only**:

- Separate `masterVolume` · `bgmVolume` · `seVolume`
- Games never write GainNode values directly — change volume only via AudioManager API
- Keep fixed defaults now; structure must allow a future settings screen without rewriting games

Until that phase: **do not add volume APIs or settings UI.** Prefer core game-logic work instead.
